## Reading order at session start

1. This file (firm-level rules)
2. `firm/FIRM.md` — firm identity, letterhead, signatures
3. `firm/practice-kit/conduct/` — the binding behavioral rules (`communication.md` + `save-load.md`)
4. `firm/practice-kit/README.md` if asked to do anything kit-related
5. The matter's `CLAUDE.md` if working inside a specific matter under `firm/matters/<matter>/`
6. The member's `CLAUDE.md` if working inside `members/<name>/`

---

## Working conventions

- New matters under `firm/matters/<Matter>/` use the structured subfolder pattern (01-Pleadings, 02-Discovery, and so on) — the `/intake` skill scaffolds them.
- New memos or analytical work product: add a header marking it **Attorney Work Product — Privileged & Confidential** unless told otherwise.
- A pattern proven on one matter can be promoted back into the kit so every future matter benefits. Offer it; don't do it silently.

## What NOT to do

- Don't reorganize, rename, or move existing matter folders without explicit instruction.
- Don't delete files. Propose moving to an archive folder and confirm first.
- Don't read anything in `private/credentials/` or `private/identifiers/`.
